good correlation between the TRMC results and device performance highlights the importance of understanding the photophysics of these devices, which is greatly affected by the delicate film processing and underlying scaffolds.
## 2. RESULTS AND DISCUSSION
## 2.1 Local Charge Carrier Mobility at $\textbf{\textit{g}}_{G H z}$
We prepared the following six samples on quartz plates: pure PVK, bare mesoporous (mp)-TiO2 $\left(\mathrm{TiO}_{2}\right)$ , PVK on mp- $\mathrm{\cdotTiO}_{2}$ $\mathrm{(PVK/TiO_{2})}$ ) or mp- $\mathrm{\bfAl}_{2}\mathrm{O}_{3}$ $\mathrm{(PVK/Al_{2}O_{3})}$ ), and spiro-OMeTAD29 coated PVK on both mp- $\mathrm{TiO}_{2}$ and mp- ${\bf A l}_{2}{\bf O}_{3}$ (Spiro/PVK/TiO2 and Spiro/PVK $\mathrm{\langleAl_{2}O_{3}\rangle}$ ). Note that the insulating mp${\mathrm{Al}}_{2}{\mathrm{O}}_{3}$ layer was confirmed to be completely unresponsive to laser-flash TRMC. Figure 1a shows the maximum $\phi\Sigma\mu\ (\phi\Sigma\mu_{\mathrm{max}})$ of the TRMC transients, monitored at 9.1 GHz, versus the incident laser intensity, $I_{0}$ , from $10^{10}$ to $10^{15}$ photons $\mathrm{cm}^{-2}$ . The transient decays of $\phi\Sigma\mu$ at various $I_{0}$ values are displayed in Figure S1 of the Supporting Information. $\phi$ and $\Sigma\mu$ are the charge carrier generation efficiency and the sum of the positive and negative charge carrier mobilities $(\mu_{+}+\mu_{-})$ , respectively. The PVK samples, regardless of the presence of $\mathrm{\mp{-}T i O}_{2}$ and mp- ${\bf\cdot A l}_{2}{\bf O}_{3}$ , exhibited exceptionally high $\phi\Sigma\mu_{\mathrm{max}}$ values in comparison to bare mp- $\mathrm{\cdotTiO}_{2}$ and a typical bulk heterojunction (a blend of poly(3- hexylthiophene) (P3HT) and phenyl- $C_{61}$ -butyric acid methyl ester (PCBM)). For both PVK and $\mathrm{PVK}/\mathrm{TiO}_{2}$ , $\phi\Sigma\mu_{\mathrm{max}}$ increased with decreasing $I_{0}$ as a result of reduced charge recombination at lower $I_{0}$ . Surprisingly, their $\phi\Sigma\mu_{\mathrm{max}}$ , also regarded as their minimum mobility, reached ca. $20~\mathrm{cm}^{2}\mathrm{V}^{-1}\mathrm{s}^{-1}$ at the lowest $I_{0}$ ${\sim}10^{10}$ photons $\mathrm{cm}^{-2}$ ), indicating that in both of these samples, PVK was behaving as an excellent photoactive layer (Table 1). This value exceeded those of P3HT:PCBM $(0.22\ \mathrm{cm}^{2}\mathrm{V}^{-1}\mathrm{s}^{-1})^{30}$ and bare mp- $\cdot\mathrm{TiO}_{2}$ $(0.066~\mathrm{cm}^{2}\mathrm{V}^{-1}\mathrm{s}^{-1}$ , consistent with literature values31,32) by several orders of magnitude. $\phi\Sigma\mu_{\mathrm{max}}$ of $\mathrm{PVK}/\mathrm{Al}_{2}\mathrm{O}_{3}$ was ca. $10\mathrm{cm}^{2}\mathrm{V}^{-1}\mathrm{s}^{-1}$ at the lowest $I_{0}$ , which is close to the THz local mobilities of $\mathrm{PVK}/\mathrm{Al}_{2}\mathrm{O}_{3}$ determined by Herz et al. $(8.1\ \mathrm{cm}^{2}\mathrm{V}^{-1}\mathrm{s}^{-1})$ and Ponseca et al. $(20\mathrm{cm}^{2}\mathrm{V}^{-1}\mathrm{s}^{-1})$ .26 Though, for a
## Journal of the American Chemical Society
more exact comparison, we should state that the mobility of our $\mathrm{PVK}/\mathrm{Al}_{2}\mathrm{O}_{3}$ was half of that found in the work of Ponseca et al.26 In contrast, our value for $\mathrm{PVK}/\mathrm{TiO}_{2}$ $(20\mathrm{cm}^{2}\mathrm{V}^{-1}\mathrm{s}^{-1})$ was 2.7 times larger than that of the latter report (Ponseca et al., $7.5\mathrm{cm}^{2}\mathrm{V}^{-1}\mathrm{s}^{-1},$ ),26 while the mobilities of pure PVK in both studies were the same $(20\mathrm{cm}^{2}\mathrm{V}^{-1}\mathrm{s}^{-1})$ ).26 It should be noted that the PVK layers of the previous THz studies were prepared by a single step method from a solution of $\mathrm{Pb}\mathrm{I}_{2}$ and excess $\mathrm{CH}_{3}\mathrm{NH}_{3}\mathrm{I}$ (e.g. in a ratio of 1:3),24,26 while our preparation adopted a two-step sequential deposition method using a DMF solution of PbI2 followed by dipping into an IPA solution of $\mathrm{CH}_{3}\mathrm{NH}_{3}\mathrm{I}$ .10 In the early days of perovskite solar cell research, $\mathrm{PVK}/\mathrm{Al}_{2}\mathrm{O}_{3}$ devices based on the one-step procedure provided higher device outputs than $\mathrm{PVK}/\mathrm{TiO}_{2}$ devices,3 in accordance with the THz mobilities reported by Ponseca et al.26 On the other hand, recent $\mathrm{PVK}/\mathrm{TiO}_{2}$ devices with enhanced PCE and reproducibility have been fabricated using the two-step method.10 To provide control data, we performed TRMC of one-step PVK samples prepared from DMF solution of $\mathrm{CH}_{3}\mathrm{NH}_{3}\mathrm{I}$ and $\mathrm{PbI}_{2}$ (1:1) mixture and found that the mobilities were 17 and 4.3 $\mathrm{cm}^{2}\ \mathrm{V}^{-1}\mathrm{s}^{-1}$ for of $\mathrm{PVK}/\mathrm{TiO}_{2}$ and $\mathrm{PVK}/\mathrm{Al}_{2}\mathrm{O}_{3}$ , respectively (Figure S2). They are lower than the corresponding PVK on mesoporous scaffold of the two-step method, underscoring the superiority of the two-step $\mathrm{PVK}/\mathrm{TiO}_{2}$ . In our device characterization, the two-step $\mathrm{PVK}/\mathrm{TiO}_{2}$ indeed demonstrated a higher efficiency $(\mathrm{PCE}=9.6\%$ , short-circuit current density $(J_{\mathrm{sc}})=19.2\ \mathrm{mA}\ \mathrm{cm}^{-2}$ , $V_{\mathrm{oc}}=0.90~\mathrm{V}$ , and fill factor $(\mathrm{FF})=0.56)$ than $\mathrm{PVK}/\mathrm{Al}_{2}\mathrm{O}_{3}$ $(\mathrm{PCE}=1.9\%$ , $J_{\mathrm{sc}}=4.5~\mathrm{mA}~\mathrm{cm}^{-2}$ , $V_{\mathrm{oc}}=0.95\:\mathrm{V}$ , $\mathrm{FF}=0.44$ , Figure S3), in line with the TRMC mobility trends reported here. The local mobility of charge carriers is not, of course, the sole determinant governing device output. However, the observed qualitative correlation between the device output and local mobility is worth mentioning. Thickness variation $(260\textrm{-}420\ \mathrm{nm})$ and resultant absorbance difference of PVK are not significant (Figure S4).
The application of HTL (spiro-OMeTAD) top-coatings onto PVK, PVK/TiO2 and $\mathrm{PVK}/\mathrm{Al}_{2}\mathrm{O}_{3}$ led to a significant suppression of $\phi\Sigma\mu_{\mathrm{max}}$ (Figure 1a). PVK and PVK/TiO2 underwent a large decrease of $1-$ 2 orders of magnitude $(\times1/6$ for PVK and 1/30 for $\mathrm{PVK}/\mathrm{TiO}_{2}$ averaged over all $I_{0}$ ), while the decrease was more moderate for $\mathrm{PVK}/\mathrm{Al}_{2}\mathrm{O}_{3}$ $(\times\ 1/3$ on average) when the HTL coating was present. Supposing
